<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Satake Yoshinobu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1570–1633</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Satake Yoshinobu was a Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> who headed the Satake clan of Hitachi province, one of the largest domains in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Because he stayed neutral at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a> in 1600, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> moved him in 1602 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akita">Akita</a> in Dewa province with a reduced income, where he founded the Kubota Domain and built Kubota Castle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/satake-yoshinobu.jpg" alt="Satake Yoshinobu" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Satake_Yoshinobu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
